## Recommended Default Values

When LLM doesn't specify values, use these defaults:

### Generator Defaults

```json
{
  "projectile": {
    "speed": 30.0,
    "lifetime": 5.0
  },
  "area_of_effect": {
    "radius": 5.0,
    "lifetime": 2.0
  },
  "cone": {
    "radius": 8.0,
    "angle": 60.0,
    "lifetime": 1.5
  }
}
```

### Modifier Defaults

```json
{
  "homing": {
    "turn_speed": 5.0
  },
  "chain": {
    "max_bounces": 3
  },
  "pierce": {
    "pierce_count": 3
  },
  "fork": {
    "fork_count": 3,
    "fork_angle": 30.0
  }
}
```

### Payload Defaults

```json
{
  "damage": {
    "amount": 20.0
  },
  "heal": {
    "amount": 15.0
  },
  "apply_status_effect": {
    "duration": 3.0
  }
}
```

## Custom Validation Rules

In addition to schema validation, implement these rules:

### Rule 1: At Least One Payload

```csharp
if (spellData.payloads == null || spellData.payloads.Length == 0)
{
    errors.Add("Spell must have at least one payload");
    return false;
}
```

### Rule 2: Reasonable Numeric Values

```csharp
// Reasonable speed
if (speed <= 0 || speed > 1000)
{
    errors.Add($"Speed out of range: {speed}");
}

// Reasonable damage
if (damage <= 0 || damage > 10000)
{
    errors.Add($"Damage out of range: {damage}");
}

// Reasonable lifetime
if (lifetime < 0.1f || lifetime > 60f)
{
    errors.Add($"Lifetime out of range: {lifetime}");
}
```

### Rule 3: Invalid Combinations

```csharp
// Homing doesn't make sense with cone or area
if (generator.type == "cone" || generator.type == "area_of_effect")
{
    if (modifiers.Any(m => m.type == "homing"))
    {
        errors.Add("Homing is not compatible with cone or area of effect");
    }
}

// Pierce and chain are mutually exclusive
bool hasPierce = modifiers.Any(m => m.type == "pierce");
bool hasChain = modifiers.Any(m => m.type == "chain");
if (hasPierce && hasChain)
{
    errors.Add("Pierce and Chain cannot be used together");
}
```

## Corresponding C# Structures

```csharp
[System.Serializable]
public class SpellDefinition
{
    public string spellName;
    public GeneratorData generator;
    public ModifierData[] modifiers;
    public PayloadData[] payloads;
}

[System.Serializable]
public class GeneratorData
{
    public string type; // "projectile", "cone", "self_cast", "area_of_effect"
    public float speed;
    public float lifetime;
    public int count;
    public float radius;
    public float angle;
}

[System.Serializable]
public class ModifierData
{
    public string type; // "homing", "chain", "pierce", etc.
    public float turn_speed;
    public int max_bounces;
    public int pierce_count;
    public int fork_count;
    public float fork_angle;
    public float spread_angle;
}

[System.Serializable]
public class PayloadData
{
    public string type; // "damage", "heal", "apply_status_effect", "spawn_entity"
    public float amount;
    public string elemental_type; // "fire", "frost", "shock", "physical", "holy"
    public string effect_name; // "slow", "burn", "stun", "poison"
    public float duration;
    public string entity_prefab;
}
```

## Deserialization in Unity

```csharp
using Newtonsoft.Json;

public class SpellJsonParser
{
    public SpellDefinition ParseSpellJson(string jsonString)
    {
        try
        {
            return JsonConvert.DeserializeObject<SpellDefinition>(jsonString);
        }
        catch (JsonException e)
        {
            Debug.LogError($"Error deserializing JSON: {e.Message}");
            throw;
        }
    }
}
```

## Important Notes

-  This schema is the **mandatory contract** between LLM and game engine
-  **Always validate** against this schema before processing
-  Use **default values** when optional properties are not specified
-  Implement **custom validation rules** in addition to schema validation
-  The **spellName** field is mandatory and should be unique
-  The **generator** field is mandatory and must have **type** defined
-  The **payloads** array is mandatory and must have **at least one element**
-  The **modifiers** array is optional and can be empty
-  Conditional properties are validated using **allOf/if/then** in JSON Schema
-  Use **Newtonsoft.Json** or **System.Text.Json** for deserialization
-  Keep this schema **synchronized** with the LLM prompt
